In Nick's cover letters (and resumes), use the Google "XYZ" framing wherever possible: accomplished **X**, as measured by **Y**, by doing **Z** — lead each proof point with the result/number, not the activity.

**Canonical metric per recurring proof point** (prefer these exact figures for consistency across artefacts):
- **ANZ Plus** — one of only two initiatives out of more than 100 AI projects across the bank that took AI directly to customers.
- **Macquarie** — cut more than 50 hours of manual effort per week (real-time event-driven platform).
- **LIMSOC / Life Saving Victoria** — presented to national executives; 199,000-member, $100M federated org, seven jurisdictions, accepted as the foundation for national adoption.
- **AccessBuddy / founder build** — replaced thousands of manual emails and hundreds of hours of admin a year. (Framed generically per [[feedback-cover-letter-power-not-gaps]] — usually not named.)

**Why:** Quantified, result-led statements read as senior and concrete; activity-led statements read as junior. **How to apply:** Mirrored in the career-pivot project file positioning rules. Pairs with [[feedback-cover-letter-power-not-gaps]] (power not vulnerability) and [[feedback-cover-letter-no-role-pointing]].
